This is a simple problem. Find min, max, sum, then compute (sum - min - max) / (n - 2).

Let me write the C# code:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public double Average(int[] salary) {
        int min = int.MaxValue;
        int max = int.MinValue;
        long sum = 0;
        foreach (int s in salary) {
            if (s < min) min = s;
            if (s > max) max = s;
            sum += s;
        }
        return (double)(sum - min - max) / (salary.Length - 2);
    }
}
```

That's it. Constraints are small (n ≤ 100, values ≤ 10^6), so no overflow issues even with int, but using long is safe.

