Looking at this problem:

- We need a sliding window of the last `m` elements.
- For each query, we need the sum of elements after removing the `k` smallest and `k` largest — i.e., the sum of the `(k+1)`-th through `(m-k)`-th smallest elements in the window.
- Since values are bounded by `10^5`, a Fenwick tree (BIT) indexed by value, tracking both **counts** and **sums**, works perfectly. The middle sum = (sum of `m-k` smallest) − (sum of `k` smallest), computed via a BIT binary-lifting descent that finds the sum of the `rank` smallest elements in O(log V).

Each `AddElement` adds the new value to the BIT and queue, evicting the oldest when the window exceeds `m`. Each `CalculateMKAverage` does two rank-based prefix-sum queries and divides by `m - 2k` (all values are positive, so integer division equals floor).

Verified against the example: with m=3, k=1, window [3,1,10] → sum of 2 smallest (4) − smallest (1) = 3 → 3/1 = 3. Later window [5,5,5] → 10 − 5 = 5 → 5. ✓

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class MKAverage {

    private readonly int m;
    private readonly int k;
    private const int MaxVal = 100000;
    private readonly int[] cntTree;
    private readonly long[] sumTree;
    private readonly Queue<int> window;

    public MKAverage(int m, int k) {
        this.m = m;
        this.k = k;
        cntTree = new int[MaxVal + 1];
        sumTree = new long[MaxVal + 1];
        window = new Queue<int>();
    }

    public void AddElement(int num) {
        window.Enqueue(num);
        Update(num, 1, num);
        if (window.Count > m) {
            int old = window.Dequeue();
            Update(old, -1, -old);
        }
    }

    public int CalculateMKAverage() {
        if (window.Count < m) return -1;
        long midSum = SumOfSmallest(m - k) - SumOfSmallest(k);
        return (int)(midSum / (m - 2 * k));
    }

    private void Update(int val, int cntDelta, long sumDelta) {
        for (int i = val; i <= MaxVal; i += i & (-i)) {
            cntTree[i] += cntDelta;
            sumTree[i] += sumDelta;
        }
    }

    private long SumOfSmallest(int rank) {
        int pos = 0;
        long s = 0;
        for (int pw = 1 << 17; pw > 0; pw >>= 1) {
            int next = pos + pw;
            if (next <= MaxVal && cntTree[next] < rank) {
                pos = next;
                rank -= cntTree[pos];
                s += sumTree[pos];
            }
        }
        s += (long)rank * (pos + 1);
        return s;
    }
}
```

