Looking at this problem:

- For each point `i` used as an anchor, compute the direction vector `(dx, dy)` to every point `j > i`.
- Normalize the direction by dividing by `gcd(dx, dy)` and fixing a canonical sign (if `dx < 0` flip both; if `dx == 0` make `dy = 1`). This makes all points on the same line through the anchor share one key, and handles vertical/horizontal lines naturally.
- Count occurrences of each normalized direction in a dictionary; the answer for that anchor is `maxCount + 1` (including the anchor itself). Anchoring only at `j > i` is sufficient because any line's full point set is counted when anchored at its earliest-indexed point.
- Encode the normalized pair as a unique `long` key (coordinates differences are bounded by 2·10⁴, so `(dx+20000)*40001 + (dy+20000)` is unique and fits easily).

Complexity is O(n² log C) with n ≤ 300, which is trivial. Points are guaranteed unique, so `dx = dy = 0` never occurs (still guarded in gcd).

Verified against both examples: example 1 gives 3 (all slope 1/1 from anchor (1,1)); example 2 gives 4 via the line (1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1) found when anchored at (3,2), where all three other points normalize to direction (1,-1).

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MaxPoints(int[][] points) {
        int n = points.Length;
        if (n <= 2) return n;
        int best = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            var count = new Dictionary<long, int>();
            int localMax = 0;
            int xi = points[i][0], yi = points[i][1];
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                int dx = points[j][0] - xi;
                int dy = points[j][1] - yi;
                int g = Gcd(dx, dy);
                dx /= g;
                dy /= g;
                if (dx < 0 || (dx == 0 && dy < 0)) { dx = -dx; dy = -dy; }
                long key = (long)(dx + 20000) * 40001 + (dy + 20000);
                int c;
                count.TryGetValue(key, out c);
                count[key] = c + 1;
                if (c + 1 > localMax) localMax = c + 1;
            }
            if (localMax + 1 > best) best = localMax + 1;
        }
        return best;
    }

    private int Gcd(int a, int b) {
        if (a < 0) a = -a;
        if (b < 0) b = -b;
        while (b != 0) {
            int t = a % b;
            a = b;
            b = t;
        }
        return a == 0 ? 1 : a;
    }
}
```

