Approach: precompute squares c² for c in 1..n into a HashSet. Then for each pair (a, b), check if a² + b² is in the set. That's O(n²) = 62500 operations, trivial.

Let me write it:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int CountTriples(int n) {
        var squares = new HashSet<int>();
        for (int c = 1; c <= n; c++) squares.Add(c * c);
        int count = 0;
        for (int a = 1; a <= n; a++) {
            for (int b = 1; b <= n; b++) {
                if (squares.Contains(a * a + b * b)) count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

