Let me analyze this problem:

1. Find the maximum bitwise OR of all elements in nums (OR of all elements gives the maximum).
2. Count the number of non-empty subsets whose OR equals this maximum.

Since nums.length <= 16, we can enumerate all 2^16 = 65536 subsets. For each subset, compute the OR and count if it equals the max.

Alternatively, use DFS/backtracking with pruning.

Simple approach:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int CountMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        int max = 0;
        foreach (var n in nums) max |= n;
        int count = 0;
        int n = nums.Length;
        for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {
            int or = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) or |= nums[i];
            }
            if (or == max) count++;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

This is O(2^n * n) = 65536 * 16 ≈ 1M operations, fine.

Or a DFS approach:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    private int maxOr, count;
    private int[] nums;

    public int CountMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        this.nums = nums;
        foreach (var n in nums) maxOr |= n;
        Dfs(0, 0);
        return count;
    }

    private void Dfs(int i, int cur) {
        if (i == nums.Length) {
            if (cur == maxOr) count++;
            return;
        }
        Dfs(i + 1, cur | nums[i]);
        Dfs(i + 1, cur);
    }
}
```

