Let me analyze this problem:

1. We need to find substrings that contain ONLY vowels AND all five vowels must be present.

Approach: Since word.length <= 100, we can use a brute force O(n²) approach:
- For each starting index i, extend to the right as long as characters are vowels.
- Track which vowels are seen using a bitmask or a set.
- When all 5 vowels are seen, count the substring (and every extension of it that stays within vowels).

Let me write the code:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int CountVowelSubstrings(string word) {
        int n = word.Length;
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int mask = 0;
            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                char c = word[j];
                if (c == 'a') mask |= 1;
                else if (c == 'e') mask |= 2;
                else if (c == 'i') mask |= 4;
                else if (c == 'o') mask |= 8;
                else if (c == 'u') mask |= 16;
                else break; // non-vowel, stop extending

                if (mask == 31) count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

