This is a classic bitmask DP problem. m, n ≤ 8, so we can use bitmasks over columns.

DP over rows: dp[mask] = max students in current row given the current row's seating mask is `mask` (valid: no two adjacent students, only on available seats, and no conflicts with previous row's upper-left/upper-right).

Standard approach: dp[i][mask] = maximum students considering rows 0..i with row i having seating arrangement `mask`. Transition: dp[i][mask] = popcount(mask) + max over prev masks pmask such that (mask & (pmask << 1)) == 0 and (mask & (pmask >> 1)) == 0.

Constraints on mask: mask must be subset of valid seats in row i, and mask & (mask << 1) == 0 (no adjacent).

We can precompute for each row the list of valid masks (subsets of available seats with no two adjacent). For n ≤ 8, that's at most Fibonacci-ish count, small (F(10) ≈ 55 or so). Actually number of independent subsets of an 8-element path is Fibonacci(10) = 55. So per row at most 55 valid masks. Then DP is 8 rows × 55 × 55 = ~24k operations. Trivial.

Alternative: iterate all 256 masks and check validity. Also fine.

Let me write:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MaxStudents(char[][] seats) {
        int m = seats.Length, n = seats[0].Length;
        // valid masks per row
        var valid = new List<int>[m];
        int[] avail = new int[m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            avail[i] = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
                if (seats[i][j] == '.') avail[i] |= 1 << j;
            valid[i] = new List<int>();
            for (int mask = avail[i]; ; mask = (mask - 1) & avail[i]) {
                if ((mask & (mask << 1)) == 0) valid[i].Add(mask);
                if (mask == 0) break;
            }
        }
        // dp
        var dp = new Dictionary<int,int>(); // or array of size 256
        int[] cur = new int[1 << n];
        // initialize with -infinity
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            var next = new int[1 << n];
            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << n); k++) next[k] = -1;
            foreach (var mask in valid[i]) {
                int best = -1;
                if (i == 0) best = 0;
                else {
                    foreach (var pmask in valid[i-1]) {
                        if (cur[pmask] < 0) continue;
                        if ((mask & (pmask << 1)) != 0) continue;
                        if ((mask & (pmask >> 1)) != 0) continue;
                        best = Math.Max(best, cur[pmask]);
                    }
                }
                if (best >= 0) next[mask] = best + BitCount(mask);
            }
            cur = next;
        }
        int ans = 0;
        foreach (var v in cur) ans = Math.Max(ans, v);
