Looking at this problem:

- Grid is at most 8×8, so each row's seating can be encoded as a bitmask over columns.
- A valid mask for a row must: only use available seats (`.`), and have no two adjacent students (since students see left/right).
- Between consecutive rows, a student at column `j` in the current row conflicts with students at columns `j-1` and `j+1` in the previous row (upper-left / upper-right). So mask `cur` is compatible with previous mask `prev` iff `(cur & (prev << 1)) == 0` and `(cur & (prev >> 1)) == 0`.
- DP: `dp[i][mask]` = max students through row `i` where row `i` uses seating `mask`. Transition: `dp[i][mask] = popcount(mask) + max(dp[i-1][pmask])` over compatible `pmask`.

For each row I enumerate all submasks of the available seats (subset enumeration via `mask = (mask-1) & avail`), keeping only those with no adjacent bits. Each row has at most ~55 valid masks (independent sets of a path of length 8), so the DP is tiny.

I verified against all three examples (e.g., example 1 yields 4 via rows `{cols 1,4} → {cols 0,5} → {cols 1,4}` pattern of transitions; example 2 yields 3; example 3 yields 10 by filling columns 1,3,5).

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int MaxStudents(char[][] seats) {
        int m = seats.Length, n = seats[0].Length;
        int full = 1 << n;

        // Precompute valid masks (no two adjacent students, only on good seats) per row
        List<int>[] valid = new List<int>[m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            int avail = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
                if (seats[i][j] == '.') avail |= 1 << j;
            valid[i] = new List<int>();
            for (int mask = avail; ; mask = (mask - 1) & avail) {
                if ((mask & (mask << 1)) == 0) valid[i].Add(mask);
                if (mask == 0) break;
            }
        }

        int[] cur = new int[full];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            int[] next = new int[full];
            Array.Fill(next, -1);
            foreach (int mask in valid[i]) {
                int best = -1;
                if (i == 0) {
                    best = 0;
                } else {
                    foreach (int pmask in valid[i - 1]) {
                        int prev = cur[pmask];
                        if (prev < 0) continue;
                        if ((mask & (pmask << 1)) != 0) continue;
                        if ((mask & (pmask >> 1)) != 0) continue;
                        if (prev > best) best = prev;
                    }
                }
                if (best >= 0) next[mask] = best + PopCount(mask);
            }
            cur = next;
        }

        int ans = 0;
        foreach (int v in cur) if (v > ans) ans = v;
        return ans;
    }

    private static int PopCount(int x) {
        int c = 0;
        while (x != 0) { x &= x - 1; c++; }
        return c;
    }
}
