This is a classic problem: minimum cost to reach destination within a time budget. The standard approach is Dijkstra with state (city, time), where cost is the sum of passing fees. Since maxTime ≤ 1000 and times are integers ≥ 1, we can do DP over (city, time) or Dijkstra where we track for each city the best cost for each time, or track best time for a given cost.

Approach: DP where dp[t][city] = minimum cost to be at city at exactly time t (or at most time t). Since maxTime ≤ 1000, we can do dp[city][t] with t from 0 to maxTime. Transition: for each edge from city, dp[city + edge.time][other] = min(dp[city][t] + fee[other]).

Complexity: O(maxTime * E) = 1000 * 1000 = 10^6, fine.

Alternative: Dijkstra with priority queue on (cost, time) pairs, with visited array of size n * (maxTime+1) or track best time per cost. Actually a common trick: Dijkstra where state is (node, time), priority is cost. Use dist[node, time] = min cost. Or simpler: since we want min cost, and among equal costs prefer min time, we can use a visited array where visited[node] stores the set of times visited... Actually the standard accepted solution: Dijkstra with dist[node] = min cost, but that's not correct because a higher-cost path might allow reaching within time. The correct approach: dp over time.

Let me implement DP:

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MinCost(int maxTime, int[][] edges, int[] passingFees) {
        int n = passingFees.Length;
        // build adjacency list
        var adj = new List<(int to, int time)>[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) adj[i] = new List<(int, int)>();
        foreach (var e in edges) {
            adj[e[0]].Add((e[1], e[2]));
            adj[e[1]].Add((e[0], e[2]));
        }
        int INF = int.MaxValue;
        // dp[t][city] = min cost to be at city at time t
        // We'll iterate time from 0 to maxTime
        var dp = new int[maxTime + 1, n];
        for (int t = 0; t <= maxTime; t++)
            for (int c = 0; c < n; c++)
                dp[t, c] = INF;
        dp[0, 0] = passingFees[0];
        int ans = INF;
        for (int t = 0; t <= maxTime; t++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {
                if (dp[t, c] == INF) continue;
                if (c == n - 1) ans = Math.Min(ans, dp[t, c]);
                foreach (var (to, time) in adj[c]) {
                    int nt = t + time;
                    if (nt > maxTime) continue;
                    int nc = dp[t, c] + passingFees[to];
                    if (nc < dp[nt, to]) dp[nt, to] = nc;
                }
            }
        }
        return ans == INF ? -1 : ans;
    }
