Looking at this problem:

**Key insight:** Each round, you pick a slice and its two neighbors are removed (3 slices gone per round). After n rounds, the n slices you picked must be pairwise non-adjacent in the original circle (if you picked slice x, its original neighbors get removed by Alice/Bob and can never be picked later). Conversely, any n non-adjacent slices in the circle can be achieved by a suitable picking order.

So the problem reduces to: **choose exactly n non-adjacent elements from a circular array of 3n elements with maximum sum.**

Since 0 and 3n-1 are adjacent in the circle, an optimal set misses at least one of them. So solve two linear cases (drop last element, drop first element) and take the max.

For a linear array, use DP: `dp[i][j]` = max sum picking exactly `j` non-adjacent elements from the first `i` elements:
- `dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-2][j-1] + s[i-1])` (skip element i-1, or take it and skip i-2).

Base cases: `dp[0][0]=0`, `dp[0][j>0]= -inf`, `dp[1][1]=s[0]`, `dp[1][j>1]= -inf`. Use a large negative sentinel for infeasible states (no overflow since chains add at most ~166·1000).

Verified against both examples: `[1,2,3,4,5,6]` → max(8 from [1..5], 10 from [2..6]) = 10 ✓; `[8,9,8,6,1,1]` → max(16 from [8,9,8,6,1], 15 from [9,8,6,1,1]) = 16 ✓.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MaxSizeSlices(int[] slices) {
        int n = slices.Length / 3;
        int m = slices.Length;
        int[] withoutLast = new int[m - 1];
        Array.Copy(slices, 0, withoutLast, 0, m - 1);
        int[] withoutFirst = new int[m - 1];
        Array.Copy(slices, 1, withoutFirst, 0, m - 1);
        return Math.Max(Pick(withoutLast, n), Pick(withoutFirst, n));
    }

    private static int Pick(int[] s, int need) {
        int m = s.Length;
        const int NEG = int.MinValue / 4;
        var dp = new int[m + 1, need + 1];
        dp[0, 0] = 0;
        for (int j = 1; j <= need; j++) dp[0, j] = NEG;
        dp[1, 0] = 0;
        dp[1, 1] = s[0];
        for (int j = 2; j <= need; j++) dp[1, j] = NEG;
        for (int i = 2; i <= m; i++) {
            dp[i, 0] = 0;
            for (int j = 1; j <= need; j++) {
                int prev = dp[i - 2, j - 1];
                int take = prev == NEG ? NEG : prev + s[i - 1];
                dp[i, j] = Math.Max(dp[i - 1, j], take);
            }
        }
        return dp[m, need];
    }
}
```

