Looking at this problem:

1. **Compute minimum removals**: Scan the string tracking balance. Unmatched `'('` at the end (`leftRem`) and unmatched `')'` encountered when balance is 0 (`rightRem`) give the exact minimum number of removals. It's a known invariant that any valid result with minimum removals removes exactly `leftRem` opening and `rightRem` closing parentheses.

2. **DFS with budgets**: Walk left to right. At each `'('`, either remove it (if `leftRem > 0`) or keep it. At each `')'`, either remove it (if `rightRem > 0`) or keep it — but only keep it if the current open balance is positive (otherwise the result could never be valid). Letters are always kept.

3. **Accept state**: At the end of the string, accept only if both budgets are exhausted and the open balance is 0 (guaranteeing validity). Use a `HashSet<string>` to deduplicate results (different removal choices can produce identical strings, e.g. `"()())()"`).

This explores at most 2^(#parentheses) ≤ 2^20 paths, well within limits, and every emitted string is valid with exactly the minimum number of removals.

Verified against examples:
- `"()())()"` → `leftRem=0, rightRem=1` → removing either of two candidate `')'` yields `"(())()"` and `"()()()"` ✓
- `"(a)())()"` → `"(a())()"`, `"(a)()()"` ✓
- `")("` → both removed → `""` ✓

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Text;

public class Solution {
    public IList<string> RemoveInvalidParentheses(string s) {
        int leftRem = 0, rightRem = 0;
        foreach (char c in s) {
            if (c == '(') {
                leftRem++;
            } else if (c == ')') {
                if (leftRem > 0) leftRem--;
                else rightRem++;
            }
        }

        var results = new HashSet<string>();
        var sb = new StringBuilder();
        Dfs(s, 0, leftRem, rightRem, 0, sb, results);
        return new List<string>(results);
    }

    private void Dfs(string s, int index, int leftRem, int rightRem, int open, StringBuilder sb, HashSet<string> results) {
        if (index == s.Length) {
            if (leftRem == 0 && rightRem == 0 && open == 0) {
                results.Add(sb.ToString());
            }
            return;
        }

        char c = s[index];
        if (c == '(') {
            if (leftRem > 0) {
                Dfs(s, index + 1, leftRem - 1, rightRem, open, sb, results);
            }
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(s, index + 1, leftRem, rightRem, open + 1, sb, results);
            sb.Length--;
        } else if (c == ')') {
            if (rightRem > 0) {
                Dfs(s, index + 1, leftRem, rightRem - 1, open, sb, results);
            }
            if (open > 0) {
                sb.Append(c);
                Dfs(s, index + 1, leftRem, rightRem, open - 1, sb, results);
                sb.Length--;
            }
        } else {
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(s, index + 1, leftRem, rightRem, open, sb, results);
            sb.Length--;
        }
    }
}
```

