This is a straightforward problem. Count word frequencies across both sentences combined. A word is uncommon if its total count across both sentences is exactly 1.

Steps:
1. Split s1 and s2 by spaces.
2. Count frequencies in a dictionary.
3. Return all words with count == 1.

Let me write the C# code:

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public class Solution {
    public string[] UncommonFromSentences(string s1, string s2) {
        var count = new Dictionary<string, int>();
        foreach (var word in s1.Split(' ').Concat(s2.Split(' '))) {
            if (count.ContainsKey(word)) count[word]++;
            else count[word] = 1;
        }
        return count.Where(kv => kv.Value == 1).Select(kv => kv.Key).ToArray();
    }
}
```

